B3 Aluminium electrolytic reverse voltage flag and reverse conduction
* ramp 0 to -3 V in 3 s through 10 ohm. VREVMAX = 1 V so flag bit 2 must go high when v < -1 V (t = 1 s)
* OHMNI BEH-CAP-ALEL subcircuit (polarised aluminium electrolytic), behavioural_approximation
* ports: p(+) n(-) flag. flag node voltage bitmask: 1 = V > VR, 2 = reverse > VREVMAX, 4 = |i| > IPK
.subckt ohm_alel p n flag params: C0=100u ESR=0.3 ESL=15n RLK=1meg VR=25 TA=25 TESRK=20 VREVMAX=1 IPK=1e9 DIS=1e-9 DN=4
.param ESRT={ESR*max(1,pow(2,(25-TA)/TESRK))}
Lesl p a {ESL}
Resr a c {ESRT}
Vsns c b 0
Cb b n {C0}
Rlk b n {RLK}
* reverse conduction of the cathode foil oxide (shape ASSUMED): anode on n, cathode on p
Drev n b dmod
.model dmod D(Is={DIS} N={DN})
Bflag flag 0 V = '(v(b,n) > {VR} ? 1 : 0) + (v(b,n) < -{VREVMAX} ? 2 : 0) + (abs(i(Vsns)) > {IPK} ? 4 : 0)'
.ends

Vr in 0 PWL(0 0 3 -3)
Rs in p 10
Xc p 0 f ohm_alel C0=100u ESR=0.3 ESL=15n RLK=1e6 VR=25
Rf f 0 1meg
.tran 0.005 3
.control
run
meas tran fl_05 find v(f) at=0.5
meas tran fl_15 find v(f) at=1.5
meas tran t_flag when v(f)=1 rise=1
meas tran irev_3 find i(Vr) at=3
quit
.endc
.end
